#!/usr/bin/python3
"""asciipaper — live ASCII wallpapers for Omarchy / Arch (Hyprland, Wayland).

Renders any web page (a URL or a local .html) in a WebKitGTK window pinned to
the desktop background layer of every monitor. The built-in presets run on
asciipaper-engine (native/) instead when it is installed: the same shaders
without WebKit, at a fraction of the memory and power.

Usage:
  asciipaper                 run the wallpaper saved in ~/.config/asciipaper/wallpaper
  asciipaper fluid           run a preset
  asciipaper https://…       run any URL
  asciipaper ./rain.html     run a local file
  asciipaper set fluid       save the choice and restart the service
  asciipaper list            list presets
  asciipaper import SOURCE [NAME]  port a picture, GIF or video (file, URL or X/Twitter post) into an ASCII wallpaper
  asciipaper create NAME [--html]  start a shader wallpaper (or an HTML one) in your library
  asciipaper preview NAME    open a wallpaper in a normal window; reloads when you save
  asciipaper export NAME [OUTPUT.zip]  one ZIP for Wallpaper Engine / Lively (Windows) and Plash (macOS)
  asciipaper render NAME OUT.mp4|webm|gif [--seconds S] [--size WxH]  record it as a video or GIF
"""
